I am trying to convert this into C# and to use with .Net Pex, but I'm getting this error which I don't understand.

"Error 3   'PexObserve.ValueForViewing' is a static type and cannot be used as a method (unless qualifying it with a type name)."

Not sure what this error message means and how to correct it.

A: PexObserve.ValueForViewing is a method of the PexFramework namespace hence you need to prefix it with PexFramework. For example:
PexFramework.PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);

You need to do the same with all other calls to PexObserve.ValueForViewing.
However, please note PexObserve is part of the Microsoft.Pex.Framework. It seems you have not added this namespace in your project. Add it to your using statements.
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;

Also, make sure you are targeting the .NET 4.5 and have all the required Pex libraries installed.
This should fix your error.

A: I had encountered the same error message 

'PexObserve.ValueForViewing' is a static type and cannot be used as a method (unless qualifying it with a type name).

when rewriting a postsharp method PexObserve to C#. I have tried to prefix the method with PexFramework but the error still occurs.
I had added the Microsoft.Pex.Framework to my project references and the using statement for PexFramework in my c# file.
Finally I found my solution:
The function PexObserve.ValueForViewing should be used in the context of Pex-annotated code and not in the context of regular C# code. There is no need to call methods directly from Microsoft.Pex.Framework. Since it's a framework method, I don't need to use it as a method per the error message.
The method PexObserve.ValueForViewing can still be used indirectly within pex method annotations. But you can't use it as a method on its own.
Example of the postsharp method usage:
[PexMethod, PexObserve]
public static int TestMethod(int parm)
{
 PexObserve.ValueForViewing("foo", parm);
 return parm + 1;
}

Hope this helps others encountering this issue, without any need to use the method directly.
Source:
https://github.com/Microsoft/Pex/blob/master/Documentation/UsingPex.md

A: The reason you are getting this error is because you are trying to use a static method of a class as an instance method.
The error message is correct. 'PexObserve.ValueForViewing' is a static method of the 'PexObserve' class, and you cannot call it using an instance reference because it is a static method. 

You may need to use:
Microsoft.Pex.Framework.PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);

Instead of just:
PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);

Hope this helps resolve your issue.

A: As far as I know, PexObserve.ValueForViewing is a static method of the PexFramework namespace. So you should prefix it with PexFramework like below: 
PexFramework.PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
Also, make sure that you have added reference to Microsoft.Pex.Framework in your project (Project -> Add Reference -> Assemblies -> Extensions -> Microsoft.Pex.Framework).
Regardless, you also need to add a using statement for the PexFramework in your source file like this:
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;

Hope this helps to solve your issue.

